{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","created_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0acfa49b0bd88396a9b621ab725f2943a7a55a2d83685f76f7d0c3ffd52204b3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"stippi/code-assistant@ba818a46c472 snapshot 114d3c2ae22361f3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1f7fd88e40046a9b8342440fb608145980568bab792bbcfad78988d3a19c14e4","slc_517c01018a92d88176d3061bb9bd7aa1be106ca165bea2f26652aef470f098db"],"source_ids":["src_af48ddd846c15f26bb9af44635475d94","src_b3efe320bae2544289f1a323ed424221"],"text":"The product includes permission tiers and a command sandbox; --sandbox-mode offers danger-full-access (the default), read-only, and workspace-write, with --sandbox-network allowing outbound network access in workspace-write mode.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","updated_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","created_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_208fd78d53f2f3422bb3381a68eb5b1d88de69c2fbe91b5e417310d9f64f1c27","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"stippi/code-assistant@ba818a46c472 snapshot 114d3c2ae22361f3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3e0ace82c4fad4cc286646391cec315da36bda4a3bf7f45e355cdde11555b870"],"source_ids":["src_af48ddd846c15f26bb9af44635475d94"],"text":"Any mode can accept an initial task via a --task flag, e.g. asking it to explain the codebase.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","updated_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","created_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.5,"id":"clm_20c179e47db9836b54d2dc79d876bf1609cc2d97865a0bdb461879958c018297","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=inference; facet=evaluation","setting":"stippi/code-assistant@ba818a46c472 snapshot 114d3c2ae22361f3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_99ce8559b8179d5f52b85845f9e69b5575455c3406dc022e188c0434eace41bc"],"source_ids":["src_ab95da9aa3285a89928d35fb87e5a1ff"],"text":"No agent-performance benchmark or eval harness appears in the provided slices; the only test-related evidence is unit/integration test coverage for features, which is development practice rather than agent evaluation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","updated_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","created_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2f014212af75a9cadb059ebea58098da837e3b697fff680b27c768d436886288","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"stippi/code-assistant@ba818a46c472 snapshot 114d3c2ae22361f3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1f7fd88e40046a9b8342440fb608145980568bab792bbcfad78988d3a19c14e4","slc_dce4e457cd519d0c58b14fe8b8dd6c382216a3cdfd1315df8545d3c9d7fa3c9c"],"source_ids":["src_af48ddd846c15f26bb9af44635475d94","src_b3efe320bae2544289f1a323ed424221"],"text":"Multiple LLM providers are supported, including Anthropic, OpenAI, Google Vertex AI, Ollama, OpenRouter, SAP AI Core, Groq, Cerebras, and Mistral, configured via providers.json and models.json with example files for each.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","updated_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","created_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2f0e78da1fc0bfc41ed1620976549fe283a7d788ec79775052d263b8140456a4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"stippi/code-assistant@ba818a46c472 snapshot 114d3c2ae22361f3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f69306f616a870be5a7ee45c327eebc0ee3f7f512bcad3e7806aa25aa4c18273"],"source_ids":["src_af48ddd846c15f26bb9af44635475d94"],"text":"The project is an open-source Rust AI coding agent that runs an autonomous agent loop over a codebase — reading, searching, editing files, and running commands — while keeping the user informed of what it is doing.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","updated_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","created_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5623a75280fb7e9f4933641565fa609999381d70ea48def4c9b29226ebae3abd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"stippi/code-assistant@ba818a46c472 snapshot 114d3c2ae22361f3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_de87800cd72b9e6d9cdc1a612cfa10088c003a87cc8b0eaa8baeab3dd3ed77bc"],"source_ids":["src_6153364550b653dbba0bb0301fd48a4d"],"text":"browser_act ships as a normal write tool because capability tags are static per tool; in the default bypass-all tier it runs freely, and embedders wanting gated consequential actions add the outward tag via the extra-capabilities hook. browser_login always prompts regardless of tier.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","updated_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","created_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_572249c81f94a4a534489e23ea2c816840df19ec8c406752f051eb060cd4571d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"stippi/code-assistant@ba818a46c472 snapshot 114d3c2ae22361f3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f6b06e6a5298fb49488ede73104aabdcbfeff344dc857eeef4be5cd36d4005a9"],"source_ids":["src_af48ddd846c15f26bb9af44635475d94"],"text":"File handling preserves each file's stored encoding, BOM, and CRLF/LF line endings, giving the model clean text while writing the file back in its original form.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","updated_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","created_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5a63018ea5d561f99872f9d0ecac565cb1ee7447b76cffaf69283288a55d7e55","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"stippi/code-assistant@ba818a46c472 snapshot 114d3c2ae22361f3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1e5d9384e4b26d0ea7bf7db8802748ed778ce565bd7850550acf3cdf1d7d2243"],"source_ids":["src_ab95da9aa3285a89928d35fb87e5a1ff"],"text":"Automatic context compaction was implemented: when prior assistant usage crosses the configured context-window threshold, a summary request is injected and the result is persisted as a user message tagged is_compaction_summary, with a collapsible UI banner.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","updated_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","created_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5d938e80747f10f9652a61c96c58e43f2202b09ef821f23d4e3110cd61509d20","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"stippi/code-assistant@ba818a46c472 snapshot 114d3c2ae22361f3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1f7fd88e40046a9b8342440fb608145980568bab792bbcfad78988d3a19c14e4","slc_58afbade460fcd926146763d90a4646a21579608594aba4c62d34872fcfcd09f"],"source_ids":["src_af48ddd846c15f26bb9af44635475d94","src_b3efe320bae2544289f1a323ed424221"],"text":"Sessions are per project with branching and persistent state; each chat session is permanently tied to its initial project/folder and tool syntax, which cannot be changed later.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","updated_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","created_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_69ccefc9b543fd9ad05673960e50d3124e920fd39a1306278275642cd46c9991","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"stippi/code-assistant@ba818a46c472 snapshot 114d3c2ae22361f3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1f7fd88e40046a9b8342440fb608145980568bab792bbcfad78988d3a19c14e4","slc_5c9b1a38bf2ba5f829cf109464c0d0305a298dbf504893c9a8750e81468ba422"],"source_ids":["src_af48ddd846c15f26bb9af44635475d94","src_b3efe320bae2544289f1a323ed424221"],"text":"Tool-invocation syntax is adaptive per session: native function calling, XML tags, or triple-caret blocks, selectable via --tool-syntax native|xml|caret.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","updated_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","created_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6ede4fe863ae2deef43e9d0cced88c516de3ff4596a9508056c12ea6876dc19d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"stippi/code-assistant@ba818a46c472 snapshot 114d3c2ae22361f3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3d9da8175576be55be012b37fd4e07f33e56e69f18f61fbbfd84049d20988a5c","slc_bd4a54f236bba3633704f2ef45bd1b43a8968c884be30df9cfabc5ceca5b0f04"],"source_ids":["src_af48ddd846c15f26bb9af44635475d94"],"text":"Zed integration registers the binary as an agent_servers entry with 'acp' args and an API key env var; Claude Desktop integration uses the 'server' subcommand in an mcpServers entry.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","updated_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","created_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_84dacb23bfbc06e56b2a43af5f7f2e0ed13302b9deb50f50d711173ce4ef5e68","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"stippi/code-assistant@ba818a46c472 snapshot 114d3c2ae22361f3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_750b5a99010444cfa1de3c746090dab2bbbb53d0ef08f0e2c5783d54b13e642c"],"source_ids":["src_6153364550b653dbba0bb0301fd48a4d"],"text":"Browser actions are tagged by capability: navigation, screenshots, and reads are read_only, while submit-style actions with external effect are outward and gated by the existing permission tiers with no new mechanism.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","updated_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","created_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8b8f808790a1442b03d1aa98d38db6147fa7a3d048eb6a0dcf78f1c43571b8c3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"stippi/code-assistant@ba818a46c472 snapshot 114d3c2ae22361f3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_15775f90c04e7347dde6c8a3d8939576c1654f3c1d6a470d906d595703c0a3ec"],"source_ids":["src_af48ddd846c15f26bb9af44635475d94"],"text":"The binary offers four interface modes: a native GUI by default, a terminal mode via --tui, an ACP agent via 'acp' for editors like Zed, and a headless MCP server via 'server'.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:45Z","updated_by_operation":"op_58a2e388e59f4b24b91893d885751332"}
